ndled** — the diff view is a presentation mode of the same comparison surface over the same run data as HLR-1 (same component, same team, same UI surface and data structures). Splitting it into a separate P1 epic would build the same surface twice plus an artificial serialization edge; it is not separately schedulable, so it is bundled into E001 at the higher priority (P0). |\n53\t| HLR-4 | P2 | Documentation covers the comparison workflow from both the runs list and the registry | RHAISTRAT-9015-E004 | New doc topics (substantive content authoring) → separate `docs-authoring` epic. Priority derived from strategy frontmatter `priority: Major` → P1 per the docs-authoring priority exception (not inherited from the P2 HLR, and it does not push priority upstream). |\n54\t\n55\tAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n56\t\n57\t## Health Warnings\n58\t\n59\t1. **Missing strategy sections**: the strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then Acceptance Criteria, no Non-Functional Requirements, and no per-component change descriptions (Affected Components is a bare list). Team assignments were inferred from the architecture-context owning teams (Dashboard → RHOAI Dashboard, Model Registry → Model Registry, Data Science Pipelines → RHOAI Pipelines). The owner of E004 (Documentation) is assumed to be RHOAI Dashboard, the team owning the workflow's primary surface — confirm with the documentation team during planning.\n60\t2. **Data Science Pipelines classified as passive**: the strategy lists Data Science Pipelines as an affected component but describes no change to it. Per the architecture context, pipeline runs (with their parameters and metrics) are already surfaced in the Dashboard via the KFP v2 API, and the Dashboard owns no data plane — so the comparison reads existing run data and no DSP code change is expected. Validation is recorded as acceptance criteria on E001 (the nearest active component's epic, owned by the consuming team). If multi-run parameter/metric retrieval against the existing API surfaces proves insufficient at implementation time, that is fix-and-retry within E001 or follow-up DSP scope — the strategy marks no open questions, so it is not modeled as an Investigation.\n61\t3. **Component mapping note**: E003's work spans Dashboard UI and Model Registry data, but its deliverable is a Dashboard surface, so it is assigned the single canonical component `Dashboard`; the registry half of HLR-2 is carried by E002 (`Model Registry`).\n62\t4. **No priority inversions detected**: E001 carries the strategy's only P0 HLR; nothing blocks it. No epic exceeds the two-week size guideline — E001 bundles HLR-1 and HLR-3 as one logical change on one surface.\n63\t\n64\t## Tiered Delivery\n65\t\n66\tNot applicable — the strategy has no external dependencies (upstream contributions, vendors, or uncertain-timing third parties); all work is in-platform.\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b46478b67d6f7be","agent_id":"a95ba77cbc2c3a7cf","session_id":"26ddeb7f-7c64-4e92-868d-773ee0351c77","uuid":"0d3b2bf3-7604-493f-abd5-3accd5c411e3","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:51:01.381Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a299bafaffb7a7e1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
