{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f05f219337a4b44","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9015-E002\n3\ttitle: Run linkage on registered model versions in the Model Registry\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n5\tcomponent: Model Registry\n6\tteam: Model Registry\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Run linkage on registered model versions in the Model Registry\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers the data side of run lineage in the Model Registry: registered model versions record a link back to the run that produced them, using the Model Registry's extension point for structured metadata on model versions, so that downstream consumers (such as the Dashboard) can resolve the originating run of any registered version.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Define and implement the run-linkage representation on registered model versions, so each version carries a reference to the run that produced it.\n38\t- Support populating the linkage at registration time, so registering clients (e.g. a pipeline step or user registering a model) can record the originating run.\n39\t- Make the linkage readable through the Model Registry REST API entity model, so the Dashboard and other consumers can retrieve the originating run for a given model version.\n40\t- The specific property/field naming and population mechanism are implementation decisions for the Model Registry team; the epic's scope is the capability, not a specific schema.\n41\t\n42\t## Acceptance Criteria\n43\t\n44\t- Given a model version registered from a run, When the version is retrieved through the Model Registry REST API, Then the response includes a reference to the run that produced it.\n45\t- Given a set of registered model versions, When queried via the API, Then the run linkage is retrievable for every version registered with lineage — measured by: an API query returns the originating-run reference for each such version.\n46\t- Given a model version registered without a known originating run, When retrieved, Then the linkage is absent or empty without breaking the entity (the link is optional metadata, not a required field).\n47\t\n48\t## HLR Traceability\n49\t\n50\t- **HLR-2 (P1)** — Registered model versions link back to the run that produced them, so a comparison can be opened from the Model Registry: this epic covers the data half (the linkage recorded on model versions and exposed via the registry API). The UI half (opening a comparison from the registry) is delivered by the Dashboard registry-integration epic.\n51\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b46478b67d6f7be","agent_id":"a95ba77cbc2c3a7cf","session_id":"26ddeb7f-7c64-4e92-868d-773ee0351c77","uuid":"669c87bc-291f-4833-bf0d-f216205f3ad2","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:51:05.079Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f05f219337a4b44","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
